@{
    Layout = "~/Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml";
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}

<div class="banner mb-4">
    <h3>Privacy Policy</h3>
    <p class="mb-0">Alumni Management System — Data Protection & Privacy</p>
</div>

<div class="card-soft p-4">

    <h5>1. Introduction</h5>
    <p>
        The Alumni Management System is committed to protecting the privacy and personal
        information of all alumni, students, and administrators who use this platform.
        This policy explains how we collect, use, and safeguard your information. By using
        this system, you agree to the terms outlined in this Privacy Policy.
    </p>

    <h5 class="mt-4">2. Information We Collect</h5>
    <ul>
        <li>Personal details (Name, Prefix, Preferred Name, Gender, Email, Phone, Address)</li>
        <li>Academic information (JAG ID, Degree, Graduation Year, Program)</li>
        <li>Professional information (Employment history, Internships, Organizations)</li>
        <li>Social information (Social Media Account links)</li>
        <li>System activity (Login timestamps, Messages, Profile updates)</li>
    </ul>

    <h5 class="mt-4">3. How We Use Your Information</h5>
    <ul>
        <li>To manage alumni records and facilitate communication</li>
        <li>To provide networking and professional opportunities among alumni</li>
        <li>To generate reports and improve system functionality</li>
        <li>To ensure system security and proper authentication</li>
        <li>To send broadcast messages from administrators (if solicitation is enabled)</li>
    </ul>

    <h5 class="mt-4">4. Alumni Profile Visibility</h5>
    <p>
        Your profile visibility is controlled by the <strong>Privacy Setting</strong> in your profile.
        This setting determines what other alumni can see when browsing the Alumni Directory.
    </p>

    <div class="row mt-3 mb-2">

        <!-- Public Profile -->
        <div class="col-md-6 mb-3">
            <div class="card border-success h-100">
                <div class="card-header bg-success text-white">
                    <i class="bi bi-globe me-2"></i>
                    <strong>Public Profile</strong>
                    <span class="badge bg-white text-success ms-2">Privacy = OFF</span>
                </div>
                <div class="card-body">
                    <p class="text-muted small mb-2">
                        When your privacy is set to <strong>OFF (Public)</strong>, the following
                        information is visible to other alumni in the directory:
                    </p>
                    <ul class="mb-0">
                        <li><i class="bi bi-check-circle-fill text-success me-2"></i>Full Name (with Prefix)</li>
                        <li><i class="bi bi-check-circle-fill text-success me-2"></i>Preferred First Name</li>
                        <li><i class="bi bi-check-circle-fill text-success me-2"></i>Graduation Year</li>
                        <li><i class="bi bi-check-circle-fill text-success me-2"></i>Current (Permanent) Email</li>
                        <li><i class="bi bi-check-circle-fill text-success me-2"></i>Student Email</li>
                        <li><i class="bi bi-check-circle-fill text-success me-2"></i>Social Media Profile Link</li>
                        <li><i class="bi bi-check-circle-fill text-success me-2"></i>City &amp; State</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="card-footer bg-light">
                    <small class="text-muted">
                        <i class="bi bi-info-circle me-1"></i>
                        Sensitive details such as your phone number, full address, JAG ID,
                        and age at graduation are <strong>never</strong> shared with other alumni
                        regardless of your privacy setting.
                    </small>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Private Profile -->
        <div class="col-md-6 mb-3">
            <div class="card border-secondary h-100">
                <div class="card-header bg-secondary text-white">
                    <i class="bi bi-lock-fill me-2"></i>
                    <strong>Private Profile</strong>
                    <span class="badge bg-white text-secondary ms-2">Privacy = ON</span>
                </div>
                <div class="card-body">
                    <p class="text-muted small mb-2">
                        When your privacy is set to <strong>ON (Private)</strong>, your profile
                        is fully protected. Other alumni will <strong>not</strong> be able to see
                        any of your personal information, including:
                    </p>
                    <ul class="mb-0">
                        <li><i class="bi bi-x-circle-fill text-danger me-2"></i>Name &amp; Prefix</li>
                        <li><i class="bi bi-x-circle-fill text-danger me-2"></i>Graduation Year</li>
                        <li><i class="bi bi-x-circle-fill text-danger me-2"></i>Email Addresses</li>
                        <li><i class="bi bi-x-circle-fill text-danger me-2"></i>Social Media Profile</li>
                        <li><i class="bi bi-x-circle-fill text-danger me-2"></i>City &amp; State</li>
                        <li><i class="bi bi-x-circle-fill text-danger me-2"></i>Any other profile details</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="card-footer bg-light">
                    <small class="text-muted">
                        <i class="bi bi-info-circle me-1"></i>
                        Only authorized Admins and Staff can view your profile when
                        privacy is enabled. Your data remains safely within the system.
                    </small>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="alert alert-info mt-2">
        <i class="bi bi-shield-lock-fill me-2"></i>
        <strong>Note:</strong> Regardless of your privacy setting, your <strong>JAG ID, phone number,
        full address, postcode, country, and age at graduation</strong> are <strong>never</strong> visible
        to other alumni. These fields are strictly accessible only by Admin and Staff.
    </div>

    <h5 class="mt-4">5. Data Protection</h5>
    <p>
        We implement industry-standard security measures including authentication,
        encrypted communication, and role-based access control to ensure your data is
        protected at all times. Only authorized administrators and staff can access
        sensitive information. All data transmissions are secured and access is
        logged for audit purposes.
    </p>

    <h5 class="mt-4">6. Data Sharing</h5>
    <p>
        Your personal data is never sold or shared with third parties. Information is
        only used within the Alumni Management System for official university purposes.
        Administrators may send broadcast messages to alumni who have enabled their
        solicitation setting.
    </p>

    <h5 class="mt-4">7. Your Rights</h5>
    <ul>
        <li>You may update your profile information at any time via the Edit Profile page</li>
        <li>You may toggle your Privacy setting to control your visibility in the Alumni Directory</li>
        <li>You may enable or disable solicitation to control whether you receive broadcast messages</li>
        <li>You may request data correction by contacting the system administrator</li>
        <li>You may request account deactivation through the administrator</li>
    </ul>

    <h5 class="mt-4">8. Cookies &amp; Session Data</h5>
    <p>
        This system uses session cookies strictly for authentication and security purposes.
        No tracking or advertising cookies are used. Sessions expire automatically after
        a period of inactivity to protect your account.
    </p>

    <h5 class="mt-4">9. Changes to This Policy</h5>
    <p>
        This Privacy Policy may be updated periodically to reflect changes in system
        functionality or legal requirements. Users will be notified of significant changes
        upon their next login.
    </p>

    <h5 class="mt-4">10. Contact</h5>
    <p>
        For privacy-related concerns, requests, or questions about your data, please
        contact the system administrator or the university IT department directly.
    </p>

    <hr />

    <p class="text-info small mb-0">
        © @DateTime.Now.Year Alumni Management System — All Rights Reserved
    </p>

</div>